{"title":"2014 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>UNM - PNM STATEWIDE MATHEMATICS CONTEST XLVI. February 1, 2014. Second Round. Three Hours\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Four siblings BRYAN, BARRY, SARAH and SHANA are having their names monogrammed on their towels. \nDifferent letters may cost different amounts to monogram. \nIf it costs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/e/c4e33e9eaddef8a83c3017810071b068c9dbfd80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textdollar{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" /> to monogram BRYAN, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/5/9953d821307721859c206f2ec5bc6ea689f65d94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textdollar{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" /> to monogram BARRY and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/2/9d2bef9adf43467fdb0234dfc3c66c999489d48d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textdollar{18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" /> to monogram SARAH,\nhow much does it cost to monogram SHANA?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/3/703ae4e23f2ef55414255451779d42f0d2fdbb48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = x^3 + 6x^2 + 12x + 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"208\" height=\"19\" />, solve the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/9/3e94462ad75f6c4509aaa066452584e7d8918d42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(f(x))) = 0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two people, call them <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, are having a discussion about the ages of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />’s children.\n</p><p>A: “What are the ages, in years only, of your four children?”\n</p><p>B: “The product of their ages is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94db15b430439ad5b3c80bfacfef0c6499ede2ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$72$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />.”\n</p><p>A: “Not enough information.”\n</p><p>B: “The sum of their ages equals your eldest daughter’s age.”\n</p><p>A: “Still not enough information.”\n</p><p>B: “My oldest child who is at least a year older than her siblings took the AMC 8 for the first time this year.”\n</p><p>A: “Still not enough information.”\n</p><p>B: “My youngest child is my only son.”\n</p><p>A: “Now I know their ages..”\n</p><p>What are their ages?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the smallest and largest possible distances between the centers of two circles of radius\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> such that there is an equilateral triangle of side of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> with two vertices on one of\nthe circles and the third vertex on the second circle.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b216498b4cb64f29f3bfdfa60736dc769f06c7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is written on the blackboard. The sum of its digits is calculated. Then the sum of the\ndigits of the result is calculated and so on until we have a single digit. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/5/8f58fa0ed70c80d40f7ca4e1a86774f19b31b9a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2014$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" />, what\nis this digit?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many triples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/b/31b1e1af4531148cbc079023f68c2b0102c4ee69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y, z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"61\" height=\"20\" /> of rational numbers satisfy the following system of equations?\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/4/cb4f2f6c066fdf3e19a4c00b4b857b370efce57b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}  x + y + z &amp;= 0\\\\ xyz + 4z &amp;= 0\\\\ xy + xz + yz + 2y &amp;= 0 \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"176\" height=\"66\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be a natural number. Show that the sum of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/9/9f95e9fc37dc276d9cfc43aba335cde356371cac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^{th}$\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> powers of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> positive\nintegers is a polynomial of degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/8/e18453e31b8b9f4f7722777b72a0eff030a17d1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />, i.e.,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/7/dd7849a099d8a9f3c18139d930da73d6cd3715c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^k + 2^k + 3^k + \\cdots + n^k = p_{k+1}(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"263\" height=\"20\" />,\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/3/e1391390f33773f0a3a70d50b5e7958a7ad2d611.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{k+1}(t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> is a polynomial of degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/8/e18453e31b8b9f4f7722777b72a0eff030a17d1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />. For example, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00fab47c0b9d0ce398d03e57d6720129d53434f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/2/352142a90b1e4d273301f3a0a4140ba18533c941.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 + 2 +\\cdots + n = \\sum_{j=1}^{n} {j} = \\frac{n(n+1)}{2}=\\tfrac{1}{2}n^2+\\tfrac{1}{2}n\\]\" width=\"369\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/3/293d30cdd8866ae68ecbe843c07d314b8889d79b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_2(t) = \\tfrac{1}{2} t^2 + \\tfrac{1}{2}t.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"130\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2014 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 7\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A certain country uses bills of denominations equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/8/a68925d8d2ad4c40de0f0b5ca767a11392ac5097.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textdollar{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/6/b56ea73e34dca3f39183c0676e1127b7afd9380d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textdollar{44}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" />. The ATM\nmachines in this country can give at a single withdrawer any amount you request as long\nas both bills are used. Show that you can withdraw <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/0/41026d80260c3364fcf9a44d9ca19f7524dfe5cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textdollar{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> if and only if you cannot withdraw\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/7/c2718761542c165ed89af416bcb2608cdb4d9973.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textdollar{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" />, where x + y = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/c/4ec760d5fb72b1f7f6f6fd44b0ac9820fbf69395.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textdollar{719}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2014 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 8\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is a mapping of the plane into itself such that the vertices of every\nequilateral triangle of side one are mapped onto the vertices of a congruent triangle.\nShow that the map <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is distance preserving, i.e., <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/4/c74128eb6011cb3860af486283f4a176955f22a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d(p, q) = d(f(p), f(q))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"172\" height=\"18\" /> for all points\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> in the plane, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/2/eb271c6519cb12b0c91a11a2cfe8b6501e854e11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d(x, y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> denotes the distance between the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> in\nthe plane. In other words, if any two points that are one unit apart are mapped to points\nthat are one unit apart, then any two points are mapped to two points that are the same\ndistance as their pre-images.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2014 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 9\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given a sheet in the shape of a rhombus whose side is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> meters long and one of its angles\nis <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d5c45388de5c75af641c046d466de3592ffa98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> what is the maximum area that can be cut out of the sheet if we are allowed to cut\ntwo discs.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2014 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 10\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018015536\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.025 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.037 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 245/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7216/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:13797:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018015536 and revision id 249492. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}